<h1>Data processing</h1>

<div class="alert alert-warning" role="note">
    <strong>Draft.</strong> This page states the processing facts as the platform is actually
    built. The binding data processing agreement must be reviewed by counsel and executed before
    the first paying customer, per <code>docs/03-architecture.md</code> §8.
</div>

<h2 class="h5">Roles</h2>
<p>
    Your organisation is the <strong>controller</strong> of the personal data MLCP reads from your
    Microsoft tenant. MLCP is the <strong>processor</strong>, and processes it only to provide the
    service you have connected.
</p>

<h2 class="h5">Categories of personal data</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Work contact identifiers: user principal name, display name, object id</li>
    <li>Organisational attributes: department, company name, office location, usage location</li>
    <li>Account state: whether the account is enabled, which licences are assigned</li>
    <li>Service usage summaries, where usage insights are enabled</li>
</ul>
<p class="text-muted">
    No special category data. No content of communications or documents at any tier.
</p>

<h2 class="h5">Subprocessors</h2>
<table class="table align-middle">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th scope="col">Subprocessor</th>
            <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
            <th scope="col">Location</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>Microsoft Azure</td>
            <td>Hosting, database, cache, messaging, key management, email delivery</td>
            <td>The region your organisation selected at connection</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p class="text-muted">
    We will give notice before adding a subprocessor, and you may object.
</p>

<h2 class="h5">Retention</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Operational data is retained while your organisation is connected.</li>
    <li>Disconnection begins a 30-day grace period, then permanent deletion.</li>
    <li>Audit records of financial reads and write operations are retained for the account
        lifetime, because they exist to answer "who changed this".</li>
    <li>After deletion we keep only a dated certificate that the deletion occurred, containing no
        personal data.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h5">Security measures</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Encryption in transit (TLS 1.2 or better) and at rest.</li>
    <li>Four-layer tenant isolation, including row-level security enforced by the database.</li>
    <li>Credentials held as certificates and keys in Azure Key Vault, reached by managed identity.</li>
    <li>No customer access or refresh tokens in application tables.</li>
    <li>Structured logging with automatic redaction of credentials and signed URLs.</li>
    <li>Private networking between application and data services.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h5">Assistance and breach notification</h2>
<p>
    We will assist you with data subject requests and, in the event of a personal data breach
    affecting your data, notify you without undue delay with the information you need to meet your
    own obligations.
</p>

